1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,337
这是我们两个分诊 PR 上的每一个提交，放在同一个时钟上
This is every commit on our two triage pull requests, on one clock:

2
00:00:04,337 --> 00:00:07,509
波士顿时间，从周二中午到周四凌晨
Boston time, from Tuesday noon to early Thursday.

3
00:00:07,829 --> 00:00:11,242
一共 109 个提交，每一个都是 agent 做的
109 commits, every one made by an agent:

4
00:00:11,242 --> 00:00:15,765
88 个改动，21 个把一个分支合并进另一个分支
88 changes, and 21 merges of one branch into another.

5
00:00:16,085 --> 00:00:18,662
GitHub 上有 40 个显示在你的名下
GitHub shows forty of them under your name,

6
00:00:18,662 --> 00:00:21,120
因为 agent 用了你的 git 身份
because the agent used your git identity.

7
00:00:21,367 --> 00:00:22,682
两个问题
Two questions.

8
00:00:22,732 --> 00:00:24,439
为什么大多数都是修复？
Why are most of them fixes?

9
00:00:24,759 --> 00:00:28,136
88 个改动里，有 53 个在提交说明里提到了 review
53 of the 88 name a review in their message:

10
00:00:28,136 --> 00:00:30,668
Bugbot、Codex，或者做审查的 agent
Bugbot, Codex, or a review agent.

11
00:00:30,988 --> 00:00:34,593
而且到现在还没有一个人 review 过，那到底是谁做的决定？
And no person has reviewed them yet, so who decided anything?

12
00:00:35,933 --> 00:00:37,533
先看机制
First, the machinery.

13
00:00:37,597 --> 00:00:40,652
每件事从一个 issue 开始，有自己的分支
Each job starts as an issue, gets its own branch,

14
00:00:40,652 --> 00:00:44,018
第一次提交后就开一个草稿 PR
and opens a draft pull request after the first commit.

15
00:00:44,338 --> 00:00:47,850
推送会唤醒两家公司的 review bot
Pushes wake two review bots from different companies:

16
00:00:47,850 --> 00:00:49,838
Cursor 的 Bugbot 每次推送都审
Cursor's Bugbot on every push,

17
00:00:49,838 --> 00:00:54,344
OpenAI 的 Codex 要等 PR 标成可以 review 之后才审
and OpenAI's Codex once the pull request is marked ready for review.

18
00:00:54,664 --> 00:00:56,968
它们可以评论，但从不改代码
They may comment, but never change code.

19
00:00:57,216 --> 00:01:01,285
agent 停下来的时候，会在 PR 下写一条交接
When an agent stops, it writes a handoff note on the pull request,

20
00:01:01,285 --> 00:01:03,936
没人看着的时候，标为无人值守
marked unattended when nobody was watching.

21
00:01:04,256 --> 00:01:06,578
重大选择写成决策记录，标为「提议」
Big choices become decision records,

22
00:01:06,578 --> 00:01:09,803
直到有人把它改成「已采纳」
marked proposed until a person marks them adopted.

23
00:01:10,123 --> 00:01:14,326
团队的规则是：聊天是临时的，仓库是永久的
The team's rule: chat is temporary, the repository is permanent.

24
00:01:14,566 --> 00:01:19,098
提交来自两个 agent 会话：第一个到午夜刚过
Two agent sessions made the commits: the first until just after midnight,

25
00:01:19,098 --> 00:01:24,251
第二个从周三凌晨 1 点 51 分到周四凌晨 0 点 45 分
the second from one fifty-one on Wednesday morning to a quarter to one on Thursday.

26
00:01:24,571 --> 00:01:27,858
聊天页叠在分诊大脑之上
The chat page was stacked on top of the triage brain,

27
00:01:27,858 --> 00:01:30,524
把大脑的改动合并进来 13 次
and pulled in the brain's changes 13 times.

28
00:01:32,167 --> 00:01:37,436
周二中午 12 点 22 分，规划了一夜之后，第一个会话开始提交
Tuesday, at twelve twenty-two, after a night of planning, the first session started committing.

29
00:01:37,756 --> 00:01:42,646
不到 40 分钟就有了骨架：15 个来源整理成的事实卡
Within forty minutes it had a skeleton: fact cards from 15 sources,

30
00:01:42,646 --> 00:01:47,975
一个规则引擎来决定紧急程度，11 个测试案例，还有一个评估
a rules engine that decided urgency, eleven test cases and an evaluation.

31
00:01:48,217 --> 00:01:49,817
然后它核对自己的事实
Then it checked its own facts.

32
00:01:50,030 --> 00:01:55,975
4 个互不通信的审查 agent 逐张对照来源读卡片
Four reviewer agents that could not talk to each other read every card against its source

33
00:01:55,975 --> 00:01:57,646
报告了 75 个问题
and reported 75 problems.

34
00:01:57,966 --> 00:02:02,041
第一批 74 张卡之后 23 分钟，卡片变成了 97 张
Twenty-three minutes after the first 74 cards, there were 97.

35
00:02:02,361 --> 00:02:06,233
有一张卡说网络外的 urgent care 你自付 20%
One had said out-of-network urgent care costs you 20 percent;

36
00:02:06,233 --> 00:02:10,233
来源说的是先付 500 美元的 deductible
the source said you pay a five-hundred-dollar deductible first.

37
00:02:11,567 --> 00:02:13,635
那天晚上 9 点 21 分
At nine twenty-one that evening,

38
00:02:13,635 --> 00:02:18,095
波士顿时间，也就是北京时间周三早上，一个提交改变了计划
Boston time, Wednesday morning in Beijing, a commit changed the plan.

39
00:02:18,415 --> 00:02:23,798
规则引擎靠匹配词语，而词表既会漏判，也会误报
The rules engine matched words, and word lists both missed things and flagged the wrong things;

40
00:02:23,798 --> 00:02:25,668
每补一处，就坏另一处
every patch broke something else.

41
00:02:25,917 --> 00:02:29,907
记录上写着你的决定：先做能演示的版本，评估以后再做
The record says you decided: a demo first, evaluation later;

42
00:02:29,907 --> 00:02:36,690
紧急程度和去处由模型判断，模型输出上的检查器成为唯一的安全层
the model judges urgency and where to go, and the checker on its output becomes the only safety layer.

43
00:02:37,010 --> 00:02:42,600
规则引擎和对照实验留在仓库里，不再推进
The rules engine and the comparison experiments stay in the repository, no longer pursued.

44
00:02:42,834 --> 00:02:46,051
但请注意：检查器本身也是由词规则组成的
But notice: the checker is also made of word rules,

45
00:02:46,051 --> 00:02:48,637
只不过查的是句子，不是症状
applied to sentences instead of symptoms.

46
00:02:48,957 --> 00:02:50,748
怎样才能不再按下葫芦浮起瓢？
What would make it less of a whack-a-mole?

47
00:02:54,983 --> 00:02:56,362
接下来是循环
Then came the loop.

48
00:02:56,412 --> 00:02:59,191
波士顿时间当晚 10 点 23 分
At ten twenty-three that night, Boston time,

49
00:02:59,191 --> 00:03:02,854
agent 把大脑的 PR 标成可以 review
the agent marked the brain's pull request ready for review

50
00:03:02,854 --> 00:03:07,527
请两位队友来看，两个 bot 从此审每一次推送
and asked two teammates to look, and both bots began reviewing every push.

51
00:03:07,847 --> 00:03:11,218
推送，bot 审查，agent 修复，再推送
Push, the bots review, the agent fixes, push again.

52
00:03:11,538 --> 00:03:13,151
从 10 点 27 分到午夜刚过
Between ten twenty-seven

53
00:03:13,151 --> 00:03:19,196
第一个会话推送了 19 个提交，大约每 5 分钟一个
and just after midnight the first session pushed 19 commits, about one every five minutes.

54
00:03:19,516 --> 00:03:24,722
在这个 PR 上，bot 写了 72 条评论，其中 64 条带来了修复
On that pull request the bots wrote 72 comments, and 64 led to fixes.

55
00:03:24,966 --> 00:03:29,103
到了午夜 12 点半，你和 agent 已经商定了一个改变
By half past midnight, you and the agent had agreed on one change:

56
00:03:29,103 --> 00:03:31,046
修复先攒起来，再一起推送
batch the fixes before pushing.

57
00:03:32,383 --> 00:03:36,947
周三，第二个会话做出了聊天页，也就是第三集讲的那一页
On Wednesday the second session built the chat page from episode three and kept

58
00:03:36,947 --> 00:03:38,547
同时继续修大脑
fixing the brain beside it.

59
00:03:38,826 --> 00:03:44,778
下午，一次最终审查同时从 5 个角度看，找出了大约 30 个问题
In the afternoon a final review looked from five angles at once and found about 30 problems.

60
00:03:45,016 --> 00:03:47,745
6 个修复 agent 一个接一个地接手
Six fix agents took them one after another,

61
00:03:47,745 --> 00:03:52,504
各用自己的分支，每个都先复现自己的 bug 再修
each on its own branch, and each first reproduced its bug before fixing it.

62
00:03:52,750 --> 00:03:54,883
为什么修 bug 之前要先复现？
Why reproduce a bug before fixing it?

63
00:03:59,750 --> 00:04:02,714
因为复现能证明这个 bug 是真的，还能给出一项检查
Because a reproduction proves the bug is real,

64
00:04:02,714 --> 00:04:05,741
修之前不通过，修之后必须通过
and gives a check that has to flip from failing

65
00:04:05,741 --> 00:04:09,542
一个没人见过它失败的 bug，修了也证明不了什么
to passing; a fix for a bug nobody saw fail proves nothing.

66
00:04:09,862 --> 00:04:13,928
把分支合并回去花了大约一个小时，还发生了冲突
Merging the branches back took about an hour and had collisions;

67
00:04:13,928 --> 00:04:18,438
其中一次，一个分支加了一个字段，另一个分支的新测试却不接受它
in one, a branch added a field that another branch's new test rejected.

68
00:04:18,758 --> 00:04:21,723
对合并结果的第二次审查又找出了 8 个
A second review of the merged result found eight more.

69
00:04:21,966 --> 00:04:26,309
这期间会话两次碰到 5 小时用量上限
Along the way the session hit its five-hour usage limit twice,

70
00:04:26,309 --> 00:04:30,162
第二次是因为 6 个修复 agent 排队跑
the second time because the six fix agents ran in a row

71
00:04:30,162 --> 00:04:32,193
每个大约 80 万 token
at about 800,000 tokens each,

72
00:04:32,193 --> 00:04:34,574
容器也重启了两次
and the container restarted twice.

73
00:04:34,894 --> 00:04:38,094
agent 之后的规则：一次最多 3 个
The agents' rule afterwards: at most three at a time.

74
00:04:39,433 --> 00:04:40,898
回到检查器
Back to the checker.

75
00:04:40,948 --> 00:04:43,017
bot 的评论大多是关于它的
Most of the bots' comments were about it.

76
00:04:43,337 --> 00:04:48,249
转向之后，它从 459 行长到 1,326 行
After the turn it grew from 459 lines to 1,326,

77
00:04:48,249 --> 00:04:52,638
此后的 45 个提交里有 27 个改过它
and 27 of the 45 commits since touched it.

78
00:04:52,958 --> 00:04:54,736
每次修复都只是把问题挪了个地方
Each fix moved the problem.

79
00:04:54,921 --> 00:04:58,285
周三，一段家长摘要说别因为保险耽误救援
On Wednesday a parent summary saying don't delay help

80
00:04:58,285 --> 00:05:01,840
却被判成先谈钱，白白多重写一次
because of insurance was flagged as putting money first,

81
00:05:01,840 --> 00:05:04,633
当天晚上，收窄一条类似的规则
which cost a needless rewrite; that evening,

82
00:05:04,633 --> 00:05:10,345
又让一句真正先谈钱的话漏了过去，直到 Bugbot 发现
narrowing a similar rule let a real money-first line slip through, until Bugbot caught it.

83
00:05:10,583 --> 00:05:13,954
于是第二天夜里，agent 不再等 bot
So on the second night the agents stopped waiting for the bots.

84
00:05:14,274 --> 00:05:20,258
挨打最多的是两条规则：没核对过营业时间，就不能说诊所此刻开着
Two rules took the beating: never claim a clinic is open right now unless its hours are checked,

85
00:05:20,258 --> 00:05:23,063
紧急情况下，不能让费用挡路
and keep cost out of the way of an emergency.

86
00:05:23,383 --> 00:05:30,097
推送之前，agent 先攻击这两条规则：写了大约 3,000 种说法
Before pushing, the agents attacked those two rules: they wrote about 3,000 ways to say a risky thing,

87
00:05:30,097 --> 00:05:32,663
有危险的，也有无害的孪生版本，全部跑一遍
or its harmless twin, and ran them all.

88
00:05:32,983 --> 00:05:38,039
第一轮找出 142 个漏判和 230 个误报
The first round found 142 misses and 230 false alarms.

89
00:05:38,283 --> 00:05:39,926
bot 迟早也会找到这些
The bots would have found these too.

90
00:05:40,246 --> 00:05:42,272
为什么要先自己攻击检查器？
Why attack the checker yourself first?

91
00:05:45,283 --> 00:05:50,318
因为 bot 一次只报一条，每次修复都要等下一轮审查
Because the bots report one finding at a time, and every fix waits for the next review.

92
00:05:50,638 --> 00:05:53,944
一次探测就找出了 372 个
One probing run found 372 at once.

93
00:05:54,264 --> 00:05:59,451
两轮下来，判错过的 1,060 个说法都修好了，留作测试
Across both rounds, 1,060 phrasings it got wrong were fixed and kept as tests

94
00:05:59,451 --> 00:06:04,974
和单元测试一起跑；还有大约 20 个更难的，列为已知漏判
that run with the unit tests; about twenty harder ones are listed as known misses.

95
00:06:05,294 --> 00:06:09,551
第二轮里，第一版修法甚至带出了 20 个新误报
In the second round, the first fix even created 20 new false alarms;

96
00:06:09,551 --> 00:06:12,931
这一次，它们在推送之前就被抓住了，而不是之后
this time they were caught before the push, not after.

97
00:06:14,267 --> 00:06:15,625
花了多少钱？
What did it cost?

98
00:06:15,675 --> 00:06:21,839
产品自己调用模型的花费有记录：一次真实回答大约 4 美分
The model calls the product made are on the record: about 4 cents for one real answer,

99
00:06:21,839 --> 00:06:28,219
整个第一天大约 77 美分，最后一晚 27 美分，上限是 50 美分
about 77 cents for the whole first day, 27 cents on the last night against a 50-cent cap.

100
00:06:28,539 --> 00:06:32,583
agent 自己的工作在仓库里没有任何标价
The agents' own work is priced nowhere in the repository;

101
00:06:32,583 --> 00:06:36,485
唯一的数字是 token：每个修复 agent 大约 80 万
the only number is tokens: about 800,000 per fix agent,

102
00:06:36,485 --> 00:06:41,168
6 个加起来接近 500 万，其余的没有记录
close to five million for the six, and none recorded for the rest.

103
00:06:42,917 --> 00:06:44,424
那么，是谁做的决定？
So who decided?

104
00:06:44,474 --> 00:06:47,827
由 agent 写下的记录列出了你的决定，其中包括
The record, written by the agents, names your calls,

105
00:06:47,827 --> 00:06:52,406
模型和思考强度、把判断交给模型的转向、把修复攒
among them the model and its effort, the turn to the model's judgement,

106
00:06:52,406 --> 00:06:56,340
在一起推送、照抄 Claude 的页面，还有收尾的约定
batching the fixes, copying Claude's page, and the stop rule:

107
00:06:56,340 --> 00:07:01,306
做到 99% 就停，最晚北京时间周四晚上 7 点收尾
stop at 99 percent, finish by Thursday at seven in the evening, Beijing time.

108
00:07:01,626 --> 00:07:05,293
代码守住了它：最后一次推送提前了 6 个多小时
The code kept it: the last push came more than six hours early,

109
00:07:05,293 --> 00:07:09,136
之后 bot 新报的 4 条写了下来，留给下一个人
and four later bot findings were written down for the next person.

110
00:07:09,384 --> 00:07:12,281
许多较小的选择是 agent 自己做的
Many smaller choices the agents made alone,

111
00:07:12,281 --> 00:07:17,469
写成了提议，标着无人值守、未经人确认
and wrote down as proposals, marked unattended and not confirmed by a person.

112
00:07:17,789 --> 00:07:21,210
有一条交接甚至把团队流程留给人来做的一次点击
One handoff even lists, among the agent's own steps,

113
00:07:21,210 --> 00:07:27,197
列为 agent 自己做的事：把 PR 标成可以 review
a click the team's workflow reserves for a person: marking a pull request ready for review.

114
00:07:27,517 --> 00:07:29,747
交接也会诚实地记下失误
The notes are honest about slips too:

115
00:07:29,747 --> 00:07:34,749
其中一条承认，早先说 Bugbot 的意见都修了，其实有 2 条没修
one admits an earlier claim that all Bugbot comments were fixed, when two were not.

116
00:07:34,984 --> 00:07:38,749
这就引出一个问题：还没有人审过
Which raises a question: with no person having reviewed it yet,

117
00:07:38,749 --> 00:07:40,722
这份代码凭什么可信？
what makes this code trustworthy?

118
00:07:44,867 --> 00:07:47,538
没有哪一道检查能单独做到。靠的是层层叠加
No single check does. It is layers:

119
00:07:47,538 --> 00:07:51,580
几百个测试，其中一个会重放那 1,060 个探测说法
hundreds of tests, one of which replays the 1,060 probes,

120
00:07:51,580 --> 00:07:57,112
两个 review bot；还有在你签字前一直是提议的决策记录
two review bots, and decision records that stay proposals until you sign them.

121
00:07:57,432 --> 00:08:00,178
决策 0004 本身也还是提议
Decision four itself is still a proposal,

122
00:08:00,178 --> 00:08:06,542
给真实用户之前，它要求先做评估，并请团队的医疗审核人看过
and before any real user it asks for an evaluation and a look from the team's medical reviewer.

123
00:08:06,862 --> 00:08:10,706
还有 12 个问题在等你，从决策 0006 的补充
Twelve more questions wait for you, from decision six's addendum

124
00:08:10,706 --> 00:08:14,371
到要不要给家长一个拨打危机热线的链接
to whether a parent should get a dial link for a crisis line.

125
00:08:19,117 --> 00:08:22,802
所以，两天里：一个下午搭好骨架、核对事实
So, two days: a skeleton and a fact check in an afternoon;

126
00:08:22,802 --> 00:08:24,645
你在 9 点 21 分的转向
your turn at nine twenty-one;

127
00:08:24,645 --> 00:08:27,060
和 bot 打地鼠的一夜
a night of whack-a-mole with the bots;

128
00:08:27,060 --> 00:08:28,560
排队的修复 agent
a queue of fix agents;

129
00:08:28,560 --> 00:08:32,398
第二个夜晚，赶在 bot 之前先攻击检查器
a second night of attacking the checker before the bots could;

130
00:08:32,398 --> 00:08:34,050
还有一条守住了的收尾约定
and a stop rule that held.

131
00:08:34,284 --> 00:08:35,663
三个问题
Three questions.

132
00:08:35,713 --> 00:08:38,444
为什么分诊大脑的提交有这么多在改检查器？
Why did so many of the brain's commits touch the checker?

133
00:08:38,764 --> 00:08:40,897
为什么修 bug 之前要先复现？
Why reproduce a bug before fixing it?

134
00:08:41,217 --> 00:08:42,860
还有什么在等你决定？
And what is still waiting for you?

135
00:08:48,100 --> 00:08:49,700
这一周的内容到这里结束
That ends this week's batch.

136
00:08:50,020 --> 00:08:53,455
下周的几集，从下周的 PR 开始
Next week's episodes start from next week's pull requests.
